.Dd November 2, 2026
.Dt XFT 7
.Os xft
.Sh NAME
.Nm xft
.Nd freestanding C23 systems library
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In xft/xft.h
.Ft void
.Fn xft_main "const t_any *__restrict__ const sp"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a freestanding C23 library for Linux and Windows.
The freestanding flavor runs on x86_64 and aarch64 Linux and on x86, x86_64,
aarch64 and thumb Windows; the hosted flavor also covers other Linux architectures,
including 32-bit x86 and ARM.
It replaces the parts of libc a program normally relies on and links with
.Fl nostdlib .
A hosted flavor, selected with
.Fl Duse-libc ,
exposes the same API on a normal toolchain.
.Pp
Programs include
.In xft/xft.h ,
which pulls in every public header except
.In xft/signals.h ,
and define
.Fn xft_main
instead of
.Fn main .
.Fn xft_main
receives the initial stack pointer, from which the runtime helpers recover
the arguments, environment and auxiliary vector, and must end with
.Fn xft_exit_process ;
see
.Xr xft_rt 3 .
.Ss Platform support
.Bl -column "Windows" "others, including riscv64, arm" "Freestanding" "-Duse-libc"
.It Sy OS Ta Sy Arch Ta Sy Freestanding Ta Fl Duse-libc
.It Linux Ta x86_64 Ta yes Ta yes
.It Linux Ta aarch64 Ta yes Ta yes
.It Linux Ta aarch64_be, riscv64, riscv32 Ta no Ta yes
.It Linux Ta loongarch64, s390x, hexagon Ta no Ta yes
.It Linux Ta sparc64, sparc, powerpc Ta no Ta yes
.It Linux Ta mips64, mips64el, mips, mipsel Ta no Ta yes
.It Linux Ta powerpc64, powerpc64le Ta no Ta yes
.It Linux Ta x86, arm, armeb, thumb, thumbeb Ta no Ta yes
.It Linux Ta arc, csky, loongarch32, m68k Ta no Ta no
.It Windows Ta x86_64 Ta yes Ta yes
.It Windows Ta aarch64 Ta yes Ta yes
.It Windows Ta x86, thumb Ta yes Ta yes
.It Windows Ta others, including riscv64, arm Ta no Ta no
.It Others Ta any Ta no Ta no
.El
.Pp
Freestanding Linux issues system calls with inline
.Ql syscall
or
.Ql svc
assembly, which exists for x86_64 and aarch64 only; other architectures go
through libc's
.Xr syscall 2 .
Freestanding Windows calls the win32 API in the system DLLs.
Zig cannot write COFF objects for the other Windows architectures.
On Linux, arc and csky are experimental backends in LLVM 23, left out of its
default builds, Zig's glibc headers for loongarch32 do not compile, and m68k is
not supported.
Targets without
.Dv __SIZEOF_INT128__ ,
the 32-bit ones apart from the x32 and n32 ABIs, leave out the 128-bit types
and the functions that take them; see
.Sx LINKING .
The x32 ABI of x86_64 and the n32 ABI of mips64 build with
.Fl Duse-libc .
.Ss Conventions
.Bl -bullet
.It
Every public symbol is prefixed
.Ql xft_ .
.It
Fallible functions return
.Vt t_result ,
which is
.Dv OK
(1) or
.Dv KO
(0).
There is no
.Va errno .
.It
Containers and allocating functions take the allocator explicitly as a
.Vt t_allocator
argument and, where the element type is not fixed, the element size in bytes.
See
.Xr xft_alloc 3 .
.It
Integer and floating-point typedefs are fixed-width and encode alignment in
the name: the plain type has alignment 1 and is safe for unaligned access,
the
.Ql a
suffix carries natural alignment.
All primitive typedefs are
.Ql may_alias .
.El
.Ss Primitive types
Declared in
.In xft/primitives.h :
.Bl -column "t_u128, t_u128a" "unsigned 128-bit (__uint128_t)"
.It Vt t_u8 , t_i8 Ta 8-bit integers
.It Vt t_u16 , t_u16a Ta 16-bit unsigned
.It Vt t_i16 , t_i16a Ta 16-bit signed
.It Vt t_u32 , t_u32a Ta 32-bit unsigned
.It Vt t_i32 , t_i32a Ta 32-bit signed
.It Vt t_u64 , t_u64a Ta 64-bit unsigned
.It Vt t_i64 , t_i64a Ta 64-bit signed
.It Vt t_u128 , t_u128a Ta unsigned 128-bit (__uint128_t), only with __SIZEOF_INT128__
.It Vt t_i128 , t_i128a Ta signed 128-bit (__int128_t), only with __SIZEOF_INT128__
.It Vt t_f32 , t_f32a Ta float
.It Vt t_f64 , t_f64a Ta double
.It Vt t_f80 , t_f80a Ta long double
.It Vt t_uptr Ta pointer-sized unsigned integer
.It Vt t_any , t_cany Ta void pointer, const void pointer
.It Vt t_anycl Ta void pointer to __GCC_CONSTRUCTIVE_SIZE-aligned memory
.It Vt t_size Ta alias of t_uptr, pointer width
.It Vt t_ssize Ta signed pointer-width integer
.El
.Pp
Compound types:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
typedef struct s_buffer {
	t_size	size;
	t_u8	*mem;	/* counted_by(size) under clang */
} t_buffer;

typedef enum e_result { OK = 1, KO = 0 } t_result;

typedef struct s_span {
	t_size	typesize;
	t_size	n;
} t_span;
.Ed
.Pp
.In xft/macros.h
defines ANSI escape strings:
.Dv ANSI_RESET ,
the foreground colors
.Dv ANSI_BLACK
through
.Dv ANSI_WHITE ,
their bold
.Dv ANSI_B*
variants, and the background colors
.Dv ANSI_BG_RED
through
.Dv ANSI_BG_WHITE .
.Ss Platform checks
.In xft/primitives.h
rejects the build with
.Ic #error
when compiling freestanding Linux on an architecture other than x86_64 or
aarch64 without
.Dv XFT_REQUIRE_LIBC ,
and on any operating system other than Linux or Windows.
On targets without
.Dv __SIZEOF_INT128__ ,
such as 32-bit ones, the 128-bit integer types and the functions that take
them are left out; see
.Xr xft_bmi 3 ,
.Xr xft_hash 3
and
.Xr xft_math 3 .
.Dv XFT_REQUIRE_LIBC
is defined by the build when
.Fl Duse-libc
is set.
