.El
.Sh BUILD OPTIONS
.Nm
builds with Zig 0.17.0 or later, whose bundled Clang
compiles the C sources; GCC is not supported:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
zig build -Doptimize=fast -Dlto=true
.Ed
.Pp
The build installs into
.Pa zig-out/ ,
or the directory given with
.Fl -prefix :
.Pa lib/libxft.a
.Pq Pa lib/xft.lib No on Windows
and the headers under
.Pa include/xft/ .
On Linux it also installs
.Pa lib/libxft-perf.a
and
.Pa lib/libxft-tailor.a ,
see
.Sx PERF AND TAILOR .
Zig consumers link the
.Ql xft
artifact of the dependency, which carries the headers, the Windows import
libraries, and on Linux
.Nm perf
and
.Nm tailor .
On Linux every build adds
.Fl fstack-clash-protection
where Clang supports it, which excludes arm, mips and 32-bit powerpc.
.Bl -tag -width "-Dfast-math"
.It Fl Doptimize
.Ql debug ,
.Ql safe ,
.Ql fast
or
.Ql small .
.Ql fast
and
.Ql safe
also add
.Fl O3 .
Default
.Ql debug .
.It Fl Dtarget
The target triple, such as
.Ql x86_64-linux
or
.Ql x86_64-windows-gnu .
Linux targets other than x86_64 and aarch64, such as
.Ql x86-linux-gnu
or
.Ql arm-linux-gnueabihf ,
need
.Fl Duse-libc .
On 32-bit targets the library calls compiler-rt for 64-bit division;
executables built by Zig link it automatically.
Default the host.
.It Fl Dcpu
The CPU model and features, such as
.Ql native ,
.Ql baseline
or
.Ql x86_64_v3 .
Every ISA path in
.Nm
follows it.
Default
.Ql native .
.It Fl Duse-libc
Build against a libc instead of freestanding.
Threads go through the C library's pthreads; glibc older than 2.34 keeps
them in
.Pa libpthread ,
which executables built by Zig link automatically and which needs
.Fl lpthread
when linking the archive by hand.
Default off.
.It Fl Dsanitize
UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer and stack checks; Zig ships no AddressSanitizer
runtime.
Requires
.Fl Duse-libc
and disables LTO.
Zig rejects the stack checks on 32-bit x86 and ARM, so a sanitized build
leaves them out there.
Default off.
.It Fl Dlto
Full link-time optimization.
Default on.
.It Fl Dfast-math
Compile with
.Fl ffast-math .
Default off.
.It Fl Dllc
Last level cache size in bytes, defining
.Dv XFT_LLC_SIZE ,
above which
.Fn xft_memcpy
and
.Fn xft_memset
switch to non-temporal stores.
Default 16777216.
.It Fl Dtests
Build the unit tests, always sanitized, and the thread tests against a
freestanding build, which creates threads with
.Xr clone 2 .
The
.Cm test
step runs both, and
.Cm freestanding-thread-tests
runs only the thread tests.
.It Fl Dfuzz
Build the fuzz targets and the
.Cm fuzz
step that runs them.
Requires
.Fl Dsanitize
and
.Fl Duse-libc .
.It Fl Dbenches
Build the benchmarks and the
.Cm run-bench
step that runs them.
Requires
.Fl Doptimize=fast ,
no
.Fl Dsanitize ,
and Linux.
.It Fl Dbootstrap
Build the library without the xid module, build
.Nm gentable ,
and regenerate its table from
.Pa DerivedCoreProperties.txt
in the source root.
Cannot be combined with
.Fl Dtests .
See
.Xr xft_xid 3 .
.El
.Pp
Warnings are always errors.
.Pp
Run the tests and fuzz targets with:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
zig build -Dtests test
zig build -Dtests freestanding-thread-tests
zig build -Duse-libc -Dsanitize -Dfuzz fuzz
.Ed
.Pp
Tests always build sanitized and hosted, so the target needs a libc: use
.Ql aarch64-linux-gnu
or
.Ql aarch64-linux-musl ,
not
.Ql aarch64-linux-none .
.Sh LINKING
Add
.Nm
as a dependency in
.Pa build.zig.zon
and link its artifact:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
const xft = b.dependency("xft", .{
    .target = target,
    .optimize = optimize,
});
exe.root_module.linkLibrary(xft.artifact("xft"));
.Ed
.Pp
Dependency options use the names under
.Sx BUILD OPTIONS ,
such as
.Ql .@"use-libc" = true .
In the freestanding flavor, do not link libc.
.Pp
The
.Pa build.zig
of
.Nm
exports its compiler flags as public constants.
Import it in your own
.Pa build.zig
and pick the lists that fit your target:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
const xft_build = @import("xft");

exe.root_module.addCSourceFile(.{
    .file = b.path("main.c"),
    .flags = &(xft_build.CFLAGS_STD ++ xft_build.CFLAGS_FREESTANDING),
    .language = .c,
});
.Ed
.Bl -tag -width "CFLAGS_FREESTANDING_win32"
.It Dv CFLAGS_STD
C sources; the public headers require it.
.It Dv CXXFLAGS_STD
C++ sources.
.It Dv CFLAGS
Every build.
.It Dv CFLAGS_linux
Every target except Windows.
.It Dv CFLAGS_x86_64
x86_64.
.It Dv CFLAGS_HOSTED
The hosted flavor.
.It Dv CFLAGS_FREESTANDING
The freestanding flavor.
.It Dv CFLAGS_FREESTANDING_win32
The freestanding flavor on Windows, in place of
.Dv CFLAGS_FREESTANDING .
.It Dv CFLAGS_STACK_CHECK , Dv SAN_FLAGS
Sanitized builds.
.It Dv WARNS , Dv CXX_WARNS
The warning sets for C and C++; both include
.Fl Werror .
.El
.Pp
.Fl fstack-clash-protection ,
.Fl ffast-math
and
.Fl O3
depend on the target and options, and have no constant.
.Pp
.Nm
calls into the system DLLs on Windows even in the freestanding flavor, so
linking
.Pa xft.lib
by hand takes the
.Pa kernel32 ,
.Pa shell32 ,
.Pa bcrypt
and
.Pa api-ms-win-core-synch-l1-2-0
import libraries.
A freestanding Windows executable uses
.Ql _start
as its entry point.
.Pp
On targets without
.Dv __SIZEOF_INT128__ ,
.Vt t_u128 ,
.Vt t_i128
and the functions that take them,
.Fn xft_murmur3 ,
.Fn xft_pow_u128 ,
.Fn xft_maxu128 ,
.Fn xft_memclz_u128
and
.Fn xft_memctz_u128 ,
are left out.
Linking the archive by hand on 32-bit targets takes compiler-rt for
.Fn __udivdi3
and
.Fn __umoddi3 .
.Sh PERF AND TAILOR
On Linux,
.Nm
builds two more libraries on top of
.Xr perf_event_open 2 ,
compiled with the same flavor as the library itself:
.Bl -tag -width "tailor"
.It Nm perf
.In xft/perf.h :
hardware and software performance counter groups, sampling, and CPU
pinning.
.It Nm tailor
.In xft/tailor.h :
the benchmark harness used by
.Pa bench/ ,
built on
.Nm perf :
it runs benchmarks in parallel, one worker per physical core, and keeps
their results to report and compare them together; see
.Xr xft_tailor 3 .
.El
.Pp
Both link
.Nm
and are linked by it in the Zig build.
Linking the archives by hand, they go before
.Nm :
.Fl lxft-tailor Fl lxft-perf Fl lxft .
They are built only on Linux.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
#include <xft/xft.h>

void	xft_main(const t_any *__restrict__ const sp)
{
	(void)sp;
	xft_exit_process(0);
}
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr xft_alloc 3 ,
.Xr xft_io 3 ,
.Xr xft_rt 3 ,
.Xr xft_xid 3
